-- title:
--   Weight-2m geometric mod 3 forms come from modular forms
-- statement:
--   Let $N \ge 1$ be an integer not divisible by $3$ and admitting a prime divisor $q$ with $q \equiv 2 \pmod 3$, let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $3$, and let $m \ge 1$ be a natural number. Let $G$ belong to `modularFunctionFieldC K N`, the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $K((q))$ generated over $K$ by the two elements `jqModC K` (the series $q^{-1}$ times the reduction to $K$ of the integral power series `jNum`, i.e. the $q$-expansion $\bar\jmath$ of the modular invariant) and `jqNModC K N` (its image under `qExpand K N`), and assume `IsModPFormFn K m` holds for $G$, that is: $G^{6}\,\bar\jmath^{\,4m}(\bar\jmath-1728)^{3m}$ is integral over the $K$-subalgebra generated by $\bar\jmath$, and $G^{2}\,\bar\jmath^{\,m}(\bar\jmath-1728)^{m}$ is integral over the $K$-subalgebra generated by $\bar\jmath^{-1}$. Then there is a power series $\varphi \in K[[q]]$ lying in [`ModPForms.modPMod N (2 * (m : ℤ)) K`](def/CuspForm_ModPForms.html#L12), the $K$-span of those power series $\sum_n \overline{a_n} q^n$ for which the $a_n \in \mathbb{Z}$ are the $q$-expansion coefficients of some modular form of weight $2m$ on $\Gamma_0(N)$, whose image in $K((q))$ equals `qexpOfWeight K (m : ℤ) G`, namely $G \cdot (\theta\bar\jmath)^{m}$ with $\theta\bar\jmath =$ `thetaJ K`.
--
--   This is the nontrivial inclusion in the identification, at the prime $3$, of the space of mod $p$ modular forms of weight $2m$ and level $N$ defined by integrality conditions on the modular function field with the space of reductions of $q$-expansions of classical weight-$2m$ forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$. It is the characteristic-$3$ case used to remove the algebraic-closedness and auxiliary-prime hypotheses in the statement that cites it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModPForms_exists_mem_modPMod_ofPowerSeries_eq_qexpOfWeight_of_isModPFormFn_of_isAlgClosed_of_charP_three.lean

import Mathlib
